&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ranked in 2024 by the Financial Times, Moniepoint is Africa&#39;s fastest growing fintech, trusted by over 10 million business and individual accounts, processing billions of naira in transactions monthly. Our mission is to enable financial happiness for every African, everywhere.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Head of Credit, Kenya owns Moniepoint&#39;s credit business in Kenya: who we lend to, on what terms and at what price, and running the credit unit economics profitably within the risk appetite. They own the value proposition and unit economics of every credit product in Kenya, starting with SME lending to our merchant base and also consumer base. They work with the Head of Business in Kenya and functionally with the Group Head of Product, Credit. They write the briefs (RFC) for product architects and engineering to build the product and lending experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the credit strategy for Kenya: which segments to serve, which credit products to offer, and how to price for risk, starting with SME lending to Moniepoint merchants and then consumers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the credit unit economics in Kenya, covering interest and fee, cost of funds, credit losses, and operating costs, with the budget, forecast, and reporting that give the Head of Business and Group Head of Credit clear visibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design credit value propositions with sound unit economics, grounded in evidence of what Kenyan businesses (and eventually for consumers) need and in what is already proven in Nigeria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply the Group credit policy framework in Kenya, and agree local risk limits and pricing changes with the Group Head of Credit and Risk &amp;amp; Compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sure every Kenya credit proposition is validated with in depth customer contacts before the RFC goes to product architects, and that every credit RFC meets the RFC standard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Data Science to define what a good underwriting decision looks like in a thin-file market, and keep tightening it using portfolio performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Growth on distribution, deciding how credit reaches customers through direct sales, the merchant base, and partner channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sure the credit business complies with Kenyan regulation from the start, including Central Bank of Kenya lending rules, credit reference bureau reporting, and data protection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience &amp;amp; Background&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Over 7 years of experience in fintech and ideally in lending specifically in Kenya.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct ownership of a lending unit economics, with the ability to explain the full economics of a portfolio you ran and how you balanced growth against portfolio quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of building or scaling an SME (or comparable) lending book, ideally in a market with thin credit history data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience launching credit products in a new market or business, from first disbursement to scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading lending teams across portfolio management, credit operations, and collections.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with product, data science, and risk teams to turn credit needs into clear requirements and better underwriting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of how a lending business makes or loses money, and of SME credit needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong grasp of credit risk and lending economics: pricing for risk, cost of funds, loss rates, vintage and roll-rate analysis, and collections.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to interrogate a credit model&#39;s output rather than simply consume it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Disciplined at framing credit bets as hypotheses and validating them before scaling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to shape the work of functions you do not own through influence and a clear commercial point of view.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills, comfortable using data and AI-assisted tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like in this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear credit strategy for Kenya agreed with the Head of Business and Group Head of Credit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The credit book growing to plan in disbursement and revenue, with credit losses within the agreed risk appetite.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Credit products meeting contribution margin targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Every Kenya credit RFC meeting the RFC standard and moving to build with little rework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clean regulatory standing with the Central Bank of Kenya, and accurate credit reference bureau reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why join us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a credit business from the ground up in one of Africa&#39;s most dynamic markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve SMEs that remain underserved by credit despite Kenya&#39;s advanced financial infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply a model already proven at scale in Nigeria, with the backing of the Group credit team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work in a fast-paced, entrepreneurial environment with significant responsibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Moniepoint&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Moniepoint Inc. is Africa’s all-in-one financial platform, helping 20 million businesses and individuals access seamless payments, banking, credit, cross-border, and business management tools each month. As Nigeria’s largest merchant acquirer, we power most of the country’s point-of-sale (POS) transactions and process over $250 billion in digital payment transaction value annually.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;JOB PURPOSE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Head, Debt Collection is a strategic leadership position tasked with the architecture and execution of Moniepoint’s debt collection framework. The primary focus of this role is the minimization of Loss Given Default (LGD) within both the business and consumer lending divisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The incumbent will oversee, develop, and implement comprehensive and versatile debt collection strategies designed to manage a diverse portfolio of credit products, ranging from digital-first retail lending to large-ticket corporate financing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Responsibilities include designing the organizational structure of the debt collection unit and recruiting high-caliber talent. Additionally, specialized expertise in debt litigation and asset recovery will be required to navigate complex cases of delinquency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A data-driven methodology must be utilized to systematically evaluate the efficacy of recovery tactics and the performance of personnel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement a segmented debt collection framework — differentiated by product type, ticket size, and delinquency stage — spanning early-stage soft collections through hardcore legal recovery, restructuring, and write-off pathways.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the org structure, recruit high-caliber talent, and stand up the operational and systems infrastructure (collections management systems, tracking dashboards, agent/dialer tooling) needed to run recovery at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct legal recovery strategy for the department — whether executed directly or through instruction of external counsel — ensuring all actions comply with applicable financial regulations and debt collection laws.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage high-level engagements with external stakeholders, including law enforcement agencies, regulatory bodies, and external counsel, to expedite resolution of non-performing loans (NPLs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design incentive structures and performance frameworks (KPIs, commission or fee structures) for the collections and recovery network to drive both recovery rate and cost-to-collect efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously train and upskill the collections and recovery network in alignment with collections&amp;nbsp; strategy and industry best practice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own collections and recovery performance reporting to senior management, including recovery rate, cost of recovery, and portfolio-level LGD trends, and feed recommendations into credit committee decisions on write-offs and restructuring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with credit, legal, risk, and finance to align collections and recovery efforts with underwriting standards and portfolio strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in a relevant field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 7 years of experience in credit/debt recovery, including senior leadership of a recovery function handling high-value non-performing loans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience across both high-ticket/corporate recovery (litigation-led, relationship-driven) and high-volume digital/retail collections (analytics-led, behavioral, tech-enabled)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of debt recovery laws, banking regulations, and court procedures in Nigeria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with digital collections infrastructure and tactics — dialer/CRM systems, SMS/USSD/app-based nudges, propensity-to-pay scoring, and behavioral segmentation for low-ticket, high-volume portfolios.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience designing, building, or scaling a recovery/collections function — including org design, systems and process build-out, and team hiring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience overseeing recovery operations with national coverage, including a strong network of legal counsel and law enforcement contacts spanning all six geo-political zones in Nigeria — as opposed to experience confined to a single state or region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent negotiation, problem-solving, and decision-making skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills with the ability to interpret financial and portfolio data to guide recovery strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relevant Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Loan Recovery &amp;amp; Collections Strategy (high-ticket and digital/retail)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Credit Risk Management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data Analytics, Propensity Scoring &amp;amp; Portfolio Reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Digital Collections Tools &amp;amp; Automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiation &amp;amp; Conflict Resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;People &amp;amp; Performance Management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organisational Design &amp;amp; Team Build-out&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we can offer you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Culture -We put our people first and prioritize the well-being of every team member. We’ve built a company where all opinions carry weight and where all voices are heard. We value and respect each other and always look out for one another. Above all, we are human.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Learning - We have a learning and development-focused environment with an emphasis on knowledge sharing, training, and regular internal technical talks.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Compensation - You’ll receive an attractive salary, pension, health insurance, annual bonus, plus other benefits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What to expect in the hiring process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A preliminary phone call with the recruiter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;An interview with one of our credit business leads&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A behavioral and technical interview with a member of the Executive team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Moniepoint is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees and candidates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ranked in 2024 by the Financial Times, Moniepoint is Africa&#39;s fastest growing fintech, trusted by over 24 million business and individual accounts, processing billions of naira in transactions monthly. Our mission is to enable financial happiness for every African, everywhere.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Head, Operations &amp;amp; Compliance Audit is responsible for leading, managing, and executing comprehensive, risk-based internal audit engagements across operational, financial, compliance, and corporate support functions of Moniepoint Microfinance Bank. Grounded in professional standards (IIA, CBN Guidelines), you will provide independent, objective assurance and consulting services to Executive Management and the Board Finance, Audit &amp;amp; Risk Committee (FARCO). The primary mandate is to evaluate and enhance the effectiveness of governance, risk management, internal controls, financial reporting integrity, regulatory compliance, and operational efficiency across all assigned domains.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, execute, and continuously update the annual risk-based internal audit plan for all assigned business units and supporting functions, aligning with the Bank&#39;s risk assessment framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic insights to senior management and the Board Audit Committee on material risks, control weaknesses, and emerging exposures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous auditing, data analytics, and automation to improve audit coverage, detect revenue leakage, and identify duplicate or unauthorized ledger postings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a high-performing team of auditors overseeing finance, fraud management, regulatory compliance, and branch operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate the design and operating effectiveness of Internal Control over Financial Reporting (ICFR) across core banking and ERP modules, as well as bank-wide cost optimization frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee fraud risk screens, assess anti-fraud controls and whistle-blowing mechanisms, and ensure immediate escalation of established fraud cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate compliance with Central Bank of Nigeria (CBN) regulations, the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023 (NDPA), and Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing (AML/CFT) frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage routine and unannounced audits across the branch network, vendor lifecycle, corporate governance processes, and enterprise marketing spend.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure all working papers, audit programs, compliance tests, and draft reports adhere strictly to IIA Standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience &amp;amp; background&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 12-15 years progressive internal audit, control, or risk management experience within Financial Services (Fintech, Microfinance Banking, Deposit Money Banks).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 5 years in a senior supervisory or managerial role leading internal audit teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record in revenue assurance, financial controls, branch operations audit, and regulatory compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of a Bachelor&#39;s Degree (B.Sc. / HND) in Accounting, Finance, Economics, Business Administration, or related fields (Master&#39;s Degree is an added advantage).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mandatory professional qualification such as ACA, ACCA, CPA, or equivalent; specialized certifications (CIA, CISA, CFE, or CRISC) are highly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of CBN regulations, MFB Prudential Guidelines, Consumer Protection Framework, AML/CFT Regulations, NDPA, and IIA International Standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced expertise in exploratory, predictive, and prescriptive data analytics and automated audit working paper tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound knowledge of core banking systems, general ledger integrity, financial statements, and payment workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uncompromising integrity, unwavering commitment to independence, and exceptional executive communication skills for board-level (FARCO) reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like in the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A comprehensively executed annual risk-based internal audit plan that aligns perfectly with the Bank&#39;s risk framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quality assurance, working papers, and draft reports that adhere strictly to IIA Standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive assessment of risks and accurate immediate escalation of material exposures and fraud cases to the CAO and Management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High-performing and continuously developing internal audit teams delivering cross-functional process audits that successfully identify control gaps and bottlenecks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why join us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the governance, risk management, and operational efficiency of one of Africa&#39;s fastest-growing fintechs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic, board-level impact by directly advising the Board Finance, Audit &amp;amp; Risk Committee (FARCO) and Executive Management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead diverse audit portfolios ranging from financial and regulatory compliance to enterprise marketing and branch operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ranked in 2024 by the Financial Times, Moniepoint is Africa’s fastest growing fintech, trusted by over 10 million business and individual accounts, processing billions of Naira’s in transactions monthly. Our mission is to enable financial happiness for every African, everywhere. Moniepoint is Africa&#39;s all-in-one financial ecosystem, empowering businesses and their customers with seamless payment, banking, credit, and management tools. In 2023, we processed $182 billion and are Nigeria&#39;s largest merchant acquirer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Head of Personal Banking Sales Network is an experienced sales professional who owns the retail sales distribution engine for personal banking. This is a network leadership role, not an individual selling role and you will be required to build, motivate and control a large independent contractor field force and the regional management layer above it. You will be measured on qualified customer acquisition and product penetration delivered at a defensible cost per unit.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duties &amp;amp; Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end performance of the sales team: deliver the acquisition and transaction target through the field sales channel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own agent productivity: acquisitions per active agent per month, share of field agents performing 100% vs target, and time to first sale for new agents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own network health: active agent count, attrition, reactivation and coverage in priority cities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and maintain territory structure, prioritising penetration in priority cities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set recruitment targets for each city/cluster and ensure delivery versus the target.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own cost per acquisition through the sales channel, including commission, incentive and field support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design commission and incentive structures that reward activated and transacting customers, not registrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure full compliance with all legal and regulatory requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the field sales performance routines: daily check-ins, weekly regional reviews, monthly business reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10 - 15 years in field sales leadership, with at least 5 years leading regional sales leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience running a distributed agent, agency or independent contractor network of significant scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ownership of a commission or incentive scheme, including designing it and defending its cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong command of sales analytics: funnel conversion, productivity distribution, cohort based performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong people leadership skills: training, motivating and managing a large field sales team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating in financial services, telecoms, FMCG distribution or another high volume regulated or semi regulated industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel across regions regularly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in banking, payments or lending distribution in Nigeria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in building and scaling a field sales team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with sales enablement tooling and CRM based territory management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re calm, objective, and grounded, even in high stakes situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You balance empathy with fairness and have strong judgment on what’s “right” versus what’s “easy.”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate with clarity and confidence, building trust at every level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You think systemically and you see patterns behind cases and design solutions that prevent recurrence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You value compliance but see your role as enabling business success, not blocking it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivery against monthly and annual first transaction targets from the sales channel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An implemented plan to increase agent output, featuring defined benchmarks and measurable tactical growth drivers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established field sales performance routines, including weekly and monthly reviews, executed against standardized templates with disciplined action tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimized cost per new active customer, trending within the approved thresholds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Ranked by the Financial Times in 2024, Moniepoint is Africa’s fastest-growing fintech, trusted by over 10 million business and individual accounts and processing billions of Naira in transactions monthly. Our mission is to enable financial happiness for every African, everywhere.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Curious about what makes Moniepoint an incredible place to work?&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://moniepoint.com/blog&quot;&gt;Check out posts on how we cultivate a culture of innovation, teamwork, and growth.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Title: Customer Support Officer (Offline State Support)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department: Customer Support Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports to: Regional Team Lead&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: Katsina State&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;The Customer Support Officer provides high-quality, timely, and professional support to walk-in customers nationwide and customers in WhatsApp Groups. The role focuses on resolving customer enquiries, technical issues, and service-related concerns while delivering a consistent customer experience aligned with the Bank’s standards and values.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;The officer serves as the first point of contact, collaborating with internal teams to ensure prompt issue resolution and offering insights to improve customer experience based on logged issues and customer feedback.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Serve as the first point of contact for walk-in customers nationwide and respond to customer inquiries on WhatsApp platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Provide prompt, accurate, and high-quality responses to customer inquiries and service requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Log all customer support requests accurately for tracking and follow-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Coordinate with relevant internal teams to ensure timely resolution of customer issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Escalate complex or unresolved issues to the Regional/State Team Lead as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Adhere to approved communication scripts, service guidelines, and operational procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Collect and document customer feedback on products and services to support continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Identify customer needs and offer appropriate solutions to ensure satisfaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Build and maintain strong, trust-based relationships with customers through clear and effective communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Maintain confidentiality and data privacy of customer information at all times.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience &amp;amp; Background&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Minimum of 1–2 years of relevant customer service or support experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Minimum educational qualification of BSc or HND.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Must have completed NYSC or possess a valid exemption/exclusion certificate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot; style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must reside in Katsina State.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills (specifically for handling walk-ins and managing WhatsApp group communications).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Strong problem-solving and issue-resolution abilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Customer-centric mindset with high empathy and emotional intelligence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Ability to collaborate effectively with internal cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Meticulous attention to detail for tracking, documentation, and data logging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Strict adherence to operational procedures, data privacy, and confidentiality guidelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like in this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;High customer satisfaction scores and positive feedback from walk-in and WhatsApp group interactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Consistently meeting or exceeding response and resolution timelines (SLAs) for logged inquiries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Accurate and thorough logging of all customer interactions to prevent unresolved gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Strong operational discipline with minimal escalations due to unresolved baseline issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Proactive collection of customer feedback that leads to actionable internal service improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why join us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Competitive compensation, benefits, and career growth opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Support for professional development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

